chived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/24","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/24/labels","id":14236899,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A2Tzj","number":24,"title":"4.7","description":"","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":3,"closed_issues":2535,"state":"closed","created_at":"2025-11-27T20:29:18Z","updated_at":"2026-10-20T18:39:31Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":"2026-06-19T16:54:35Z"},"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-12-12T19:14:23Z","updated_at":"2026-02-27T14:53:48Z","closed_at":"2026-02-27T14:53:48Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in Godot 4.4 onward\n\n### System information\n\nAny with Mobile or Forward+ renderers. Does NOT reproduce with Compatibility renderer.\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen the [LinearToSRGB ColorFunc](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/97388) was added to visual shaders, clamping of values to the range of [0, 1] was included in the conversion. This is not necessary for nonlinear sRGB encoding and if this clamping is desired by the user it can be applied quite simply by using the existing `Clamp` node. Additionally, this clamping behaviour does NOT happen with the Compatibility renderer; the clamping behaviour of LinearToSRGB is inconsistent between these renderers.\n\nThis issue primarily affects projects where \"overbright\"/HDR values should be maintained when performing operations with the LinearToSRGB ColorFunc. Some examples are when HDR 2D is enabled on the project and tonemapping or [HDR output](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/94496) is used.\n\nAs an example, let's say I have a shader that blends nicely with HDR 2D disabled (first row of the table). I want to maintain the same appearance, but with HDR 2D enabled so that I can get the benefits of HDR output or better internal HDR fidelity. I can simply rewrite the existing shader with the LinearToSRGB visual shader node to produce the same appearance when HDR 2D is enabled (second row of the table):\n\n| Configuration | Visual Shader | Result\n--|--|--\nHDR 2D disabled | <img width=\"1584\" height=\"1048\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/29252277-b3e6-4784-a801-c88452983a46\" /> | <img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f67d1b72-152f-4803-8241-7f650a2aa1ab\" />\nHDR 2D enabled | <img width=\"1994\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b034872d-4647-4a25-82e4-1c0e09ef2d16\" /> | <img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1ccbdcc1-0658-42d0-8bec-4d4fb1569697\" />\n\nSo far so good! But the reason that I switched to HDR 2D was to get higher HDR fidelity and/or HDR output. So when I make the background image extra-bright and apply a tonemapper, suddenly the blended object makes my HDR background clip. This is because of the clipping that is included in the LinearToSRGB node. If I modify Godot to exclude this clipping from the node, I get the expected behaviour shown here:\n\n| Problem: background clouds are clipped | Expected: background clouds remain overbright for good tonemapping\n--|--\n<img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/3d76c0d5-e45f-4e26-8bd2-3195d6ddac5a\" /> | <img width=\"1152\" height=\"648\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b1a8632d-14e4-4cbe-9499-b8d73f7eaadc\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Use the LinearToSRGB ColorFunc visual shader node with an overbright or negative input\n2. Note that the output has clamped the values to [0, 1]\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[hdr-srgb-blending.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24133874/hdr-srgb-blending.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113952/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113952/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}